  "Never ship a module of invented SKUs or branches even if nothing renders it (docs/91).",
  "Never a literal $ or % in page markup; the daily sweep fails on one (docs/90, docs/92).",
  "Never fabricate a variance across mismatched units — 'Review (UOM)' (CONVENTIONS §10c).",
  "Never show an aggregate that crosses a vendor or office silo (CONVENTIONS §10b).",
  "Never pointer-events: none on a control with a tooltip (docs/88).",
  "Never find a button by position; never set .checked and expect the UI to follow (docs/100).",
  "Never introduce a token, hex, font or radius outside the system (DSN-010, DSN-014).",
  "Never swap a brand colour's role; never make gold a button or the CTA green (DSN-011).",
  "Never monospace outside Property Cards and SKU cells (DSN-013).",
  "Never mix xl and sm radii in one group (DSN-015).",
  "Never use the Phase 2 typeface before the token changes (DSN-020); never a partial font update (DSN-016).",
  "Never a decorative or vanity KPI (docs/40 §4).",
  "Never read the audit through v_invoice_audit_line; use the materialised view (CONVENTIONS §10b).",
  "Never trust an unranged PostgREST select in a loader (docs/40 §8).",
  "Never let the mouse wheel change owner except as the result of a click (standards/design/v1.md).",
  "Never special-case a vendor to make a number look right (CONVENTIONS §10b).",
  "Never mix a row that needs a system fix with one that needs a phone call (docs/103).",
  "Never store a derived figure; compute it live (friday-wip.astro:250-252).",
  "Never delete rows that fall off a board — flag them (docs/85, docs/103).",
  "Never reformat a currency field on every keystroke (friday-wip.astro:532-535).",
  "Never block the app shell on the cache worker (AppShell.astro:262).",
  "Never profanity anywhere — docs, prompts, seed data, comments (CONVENTIONS §8).",
];
---

<DesignSystemShell slug="decisions" source="docs/40 · docs/82 · docs/84 · docs/90 · docs/91 · docs/96 · docs/100 · docs/109 · standards/design/v1.md · context/memory/*">
  <p class="ds-callout">
    <b>How to use this log</b>
    Each row is a decision, the reason, and where it is recorded. Before changing a surface, search this page for the
    surface and the control. A decision here is reversed only with new user evidence, and the reversal is added as a new
    row — rows are never deleted. Dates are when the decision was recorded.
  </p>

  <DsSection id="nesting" title="Office / vendor / branch nesting">
    <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table"><thead><tr><th>Decision</th><th>Why</th><th>Recorded</th><th>When</th></tr></thead><tbody>{nesting.map((r) => <tr><td>{r[0]}</td><td>{r[1]}</td><td><code>{r[2]}</code></td><td class="nowrap">{r[3]}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
    <div class="ds-rules">
      <DsRule id="UX-01" title="Every accounting and operations surface nests PE Office → Vendor Branch → Document → Line; a new surface that lists money nests the same way." source="invoice-audit-tree.ts:1; docs/96">
        <p>Vendor before branch, branch before document. The office is the first level because price agreements are office silos.</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="UX-02" title="Aggregates shown to a human are office-scoped; nothing on screen sums across a vendor or office silo." source="CONVENTIONS §10b">
        <p>"All offices" hides nothing and adds nothing.</p>
      </DsRule>
    </div>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="filters" title="Filter rules">
    <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table"><thead><tr><th>Decision</th><th>Why</th><th>Recorded</th><th>When</th></tr></thead><tbody>{filters.map((r) => <tr><td>{r[0]}</td><td>{r[1]}</td><td><code>{r[2]}</code></td><td class="nowrap">{r[3]}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
    <div class="ds-rules">
      <DsRule id="UX-03" title="One office select, one scope control, one search, one 'More filters' disclosure; filters AND in one pass; the toolbar names the active filter with a clear control." source="docs/100; invoice-audit.astro toolbar">
        <p>"All" is the empty value and means no constraint.</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="UX-04" title="Deep links carry scope and pre-filter on land; an unknown scope shows an honest empty result." source="docs/40 §6; invoice-audit-tree.ts:936-959">
        <p>Scroll the landed node into view and flash it once.</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="UX-05" title="Filters, reveal and open state persist per surface in localStorage." source="standards/design/v1.md:110-112">
        <p>A planning surface looks the way it was left.</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="UX-12" title="One search per list, and it opens its hits: every branch holding a match opens in a state of its own that clearing the search restores; a second search destination is never added beside a list that has a search box." source="CRM repo docs/DECISIONS.md SEARCH-INTO-CUSTOMERS-1–3">
        <p>Bound the auto-open (one read of the matches, never of every row); above the bound, say how to narrow instead.</p>
      </DsRule>
    </div>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="table-decisions" title="Table rules">
    <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table"><thead><tr><th>Decision</th><th>Why</th><th>Recorded</th><th>When</th></tr></thead><tbody>{tables.map((r) => <tr><td>{r[0]}</td><td>{r[1]}</td><td><code>{r[2]}</code></td><td class="nowrap">{r[3]}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
    <div class="ds-rules">
      <DsRule id="UX-06" title="Ten rows, measured pane, cost-stating control, filters before paging, sticky header rules — the long-list contract applies to every unbounded list." source="standards/design/v1.md § Long-list disclosure">
        <p>Outstanding adopters: Invoice Audit, Price List Review, Categorize Price Lines, Credit Memos, Agreement Builder.</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="UX-07" title="Group before you widen: category sections for lines, pills + detail grid instead of wide tables, global column-group state." source="docs/40 §5, §5a; friday-wip.astro:184-189">
        <p>Uncategorized stays visible.</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="UX-11" title="Attachment intake: a placeholder icon when empty, drag and drop, one click to the device's own chooser, and Photo library beside any camera button." source="standards/design/v1.md § Attachment intake">
        <p>Never capture on the only file input. One shared component per app; the chooser and a drop share one upload path. Outstanding adopters (CRM): job library and form attachments, weekly document upload, staff headshot, job Files tab.</p>
      </DsRule>
    </div>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="feedback" title="Feedback-driven changes">
    <p>What a person said or did, and what changed because of it. This is the evidence that outranks any preference (see <a href="/design-system/#user-first">User over designer</a>).</p>
    <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table"><thead><tr><th>Evidence</th><th>Effect</th><th>Recorded</th><th>When</th></tr></thead><tbody>{feedback.map((r) => <tr><td>{r[0]}</td><td>{r[1]}</td><td><code>{r[2]}</code></td><td class="nowrap">{r[3]}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
    <div class="ds-rules">
      <DsRule id="UX-08" title="A recorded observation of a user failing or working around a screen outranks every preference; the change and its evidence are logged here." source="this chapter">
        <p>Two regressions were caught only by opening the page in a browser (positional selector, innerHTML wiping a KPI). Open the page.</p>
      </DsRule>
    </div>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="actions" title="Actions & approval gates">
    <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table"><thead><tr><th>Decision</th><th>Why</th><th>Recorded</th><th>When</th></tr></thead><tbody>{actions.map((r) => <tr><td>{r[0]}</td><td>{r[1]}</td><td><code>{r[2]}</code></td><td class="nowrap">{r[3]}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
    <div class="ds-rules">
      <DsRule id="UX-09" title="Human-in-the-loop is visible in the UI: the app records that a human acted, states the non-effects in the confirm, and never sends, pays or writes externally on its own." source="SOUL; docs/100; docs/74 (QBO read-only)">
        <p>The Communications Dashboard (docs/45) is the designed, unbuilt central gate; until it exists each surface carries its own confirm.</p>
      </DsRule>
    </div>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="nav-decisions" title="Navigation">
    <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table"><thead><tr><th>Decision</th><th>Why</th><th>Recorded</th><th>When</th></tr></thead><tbody>{nav.map((r) => <tr><td>{r[0]}</td><td>{r[1]}</td><td><code>{r[2]}</code></td><td class="nowrap">{r[3]}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="never" title="Never-do list">
    <p>Every explicit "never" recorded in the repo, in one place.</p>
    <ol>{never.map((n) => <li>{n}</li>)}</ol>
    <div class="ds-rules">
      <DsRule id="UX-10" title="A rule on this page is reversed only by a new row citing new user evidence; rows are never deleted." source="this chapter">
        <p>An agent that finds a rule inconvenient records the tension and asks; it does not quietly diverge.</p>
      </DsRule>
    </div>
  </DsSection>
</DesignSystemShell>
